    <section class="container section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h2 id="about-title">From neural signals to meaningful models.</h2>
        <p>
          Dr. Lydia Moreno is an associate professor of Computational Neuroscience at
          Riverbend University’s School of Biological Sciences. Her work sits at the
          intersection of machine learning, systems neuroscience, and bioinformatics,
          aiming to unravel how neural circuits encode and process complex sensory
          information.
        </p>
        <p>
          She received her Ph.D. in Computational Biology from Baywood Institute of
          Technology and completed postdoctoral training in high-throughput imaging
          analysis at Northborough Research Center.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container section-tight" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
      <div class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research interests</p>
        <h2 id="research-title">Questions I work on.</h2>
        <p>
          My research combines computational methods with rich experimental data to
          make neural systems more legible, measurable, and explainable.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="interest-grid">
        <article class="interest-card">
          <span class="number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <h3>Neural Encoding &amp; Decoding</h3>
          <p>
            Developing interpretable models that translate spike-train data into
            behavioral predictions.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="interest-card">
          <span class="number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <h3>Machine Learning for Biomedical Imaging</h3>
          <p>
            Applying convolutional and graph neural networks to magnetic resonance and
            two-photon microscopy data.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="interest-card">
          <span class="number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <h3>Single-Cell Omics</h3>
          <p>
            Designing scalable pipelines for integrating multi-modal single-cell genomics
            and spatial transcriptomics.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="interest-card">
          <span class="number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <h3>Explainable AI in Neuroscience</h3>
          <p>
            Building frameworks to probe decision boundaries and feature attributions in
            black-box models.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container section" id="education" aria-labelledby="education-title">
      <div class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Education</p>
        <h2 id="education-title">Training across biology and computation.</h2>
      </div>

      <ol class="timeline">
        <li>
          <span class="year">2014–2019</span>
          <h3>Ph.D., Computational Biology</h3>
          <p class="institution">Baywood Institute of Technology</p>
          <p class="detail">
            Dissertation: “Deep Learning Models for Decoding Neural Population Activity”
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="year">2012–2014</span>
          <h3>M.Sc., Bioinformatics</h3>
          <p class="institution">Riverbend University</p>
          <p class="detail">
            Thesis: “Statistical Methods for Single-Cell RNA-Seq Analysis”
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="year">2008–2012</span>
          <h3>B.Sc., Computer Science</h3>
          <p class="institution">Crestfield College of Engineering</p>
          <p class="detail">
            Graduated magna cum laude; President, Data Science Club
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="container section-tight" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
      <div class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Selected projects</p>
        <h2 id="projects-title">Building tools that move research forward.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="project-grid">
        <article class="project-card">
          <div>
            <h3>DeepVision: High-Resolution Neural Activity Mapping</h3>
            <span class="project-role">Lead Developer &amp; Project Coordinator</span>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>Designed a PyTorch-based pipeline to segment two-photon images of mouse visual cortex.</li>
            <li>Integrated temporal convolutional networks to predict stimulus orientation from calcium-imaging traces.</li>
            <li>Deployed a Dockerized microservice for real-time data processing in collaboration with Cascade Imaging Lab.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="project-card">
          <div>
            <h3>NeuroGraph: Graph Neural Networks for Circuit Analysis</h3>
            <span class="project-role">Principal Investigator</span>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>Constructed graph representations of reconstructed neuron meshes from electron-microscopy.</li>
            <li>Trained GNNs to classify synapse types and infer connectivity motifs.</li>
            <li>Published an open-source toolkit in the NeuroTools suite, adopted by 12 labs worldwide.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="project-card">
          <div>
            <h3>CellMap: Multi-Modal Single-Cell Atlas</h3>
            <span class="project-role">Co-Principal Investigator</span>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>Developed a Nextflow workflow combining scRNA-Seq, ATAC-Seq, and spatial FISH data.</li>
            <li>Implemented Bayesian clustering to resolve cell-type hierarchies in human cortical organoids.</li>
            <li>Presented at the International Conference on Single-Cell Genomics (ICSCG) 2023.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container section" id="teaching" aria-labelledby="teaching-title">
